---
export const prerender = false

// /why is the COMPARISON / answer-engine surface (demoted from the old manifesto).
// It does not re-argue that the gap exists (that is the home's job). It answers the
// decision questions a researcher or an AI answer-engine asks when comparing the
// Operator to the alternatives: a chatbot, building your own, a hire, doing nothing.
// Each H2 is a question; the same questions/answers are emitted as FAQPage JSON-LD
// (one artifact). Answer-shaped: a direct answer first, then the expansion.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import CtaButton from '../components/CtaButton.astro'

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is the Operator just a chatbot?',
    a: 'No. A chatbot waits for someone to type a question and answers it. The Operator does the work. It reads the inquiry, pulls what matters from your systems, drafts the reply in your voice, books the next step, and logs it where your team can see. A chatbot is a conversation; the Operator is a worker that carries tasks to done across the tools you already run.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Should we build our own AI agent or have one built and run for us?',
    a: 'You can build your own, and some teams do. The cost is rarely the build. It is keeping it working: wiring it into your tools, watching it, fixing what drifts, and keeping up as the technology changes every month. The Operator is built for your business and run for you. You give feedback to a worker instead of taking on a second job operating one.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is an Operator different from hiring someone?',
    a: 'The honest comparison is against a hire, not against software, because the Operator takes on work you would otherwise hire a person to do. A new hire is capable and still spends months learning your business and your tools while you pay for the ramp. The Operator learns the systems you run quickly, works across them, and what it learns stays with your business instead of leaving when a person does.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will it replace our people?',
    a: 'No. It takes the connective busywork off your team, the follow-ups and handoffs that eat the day, so your people spend their time on the work only they can do. The goal is to give them their hours back, not to remove them. You decide what the Operator handles and what stays with a person.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is it safe to let it work on its own?',
    a: 'You set what it can do on its own and what waits for a person to approve. That decision is in writing and you can change it anytime, and the Operator never widens its own authority. Every action it takes is recorded where you can see what it did, when, and why. We build it, run it, and stay accountable for how it works.',
  },
]

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
}
---

<Base
  title="How The Operator Compares | SMD Services"
  description="Straight answers to the questions worth asking: how a managed Operator compares to a chatbot, building your own, and hiring a person, and how you keep it safe."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" role="main">
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

    <!-- Hero: frames the page as the decision questions, not a manifesto -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] px-6 pt-24 pb-16">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <p
          class="mb-6 font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]"
        >
          Straight Answers
        </p>
        <h1
          class="mb-8 font-['Archivo'] text-5xl md:text-7xl font-black uppercase leading-[0.95] tracking-[-0.03em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          The Questions Worth Asking.
        </h1>
        <p
          class="max-w-2xl font-['Archivo'] text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]"
        >
          You have options for the work that falls between your people and your software. Here is
          how a managed Operator compares to each of them, in plain terms.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Q&A: each H2 matches a FAQPage question above -->
    {
      faqs.map((f, i) => (
        <section
          class:list={[
            'px-6 py-20',
            i % 2 === 0 ? 'bg-white' : 'bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)]',
          ]}
        >
          <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
            <p class="mb-5 font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
              {`Q ${String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}`}
            </p>
            <h2 class="mb-8 max-w-3xl font-['Archivo'] text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]">
              {f.q}
            </h2>
            <p class="max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
              {f.a}
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <!-- Forwardable close + the door -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-surface-inverse)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl text-center">
        <p
          class="mb-6 font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-muted)]"
        >
          The Short Version
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mx-auto mb-10 max-w-3xl font-['Archivo'] text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black uppercase leading-tight tracking-[-0.02em] text-white"
        >
          A Chatbot Answers. A Tool Waits. A Hire Leaves. The Operator Does The Work, And We Keep It
          Running.
        </h2>
        <CtaButton variant="outline-white" href="/book?interest=operator" data-ev="why-final-cta"
          >Start the conversation</CtaButton
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
